  m_Name: Day3_BoardWorkshop
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::DaySequenceData
  dayNumber: 3
  steps:
  - stepID: Start
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: Wednesday. The tiles finally form a grid. Steve has sent the next task. I should read his email and
      close the inbox.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_Call
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1002
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_Call
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_SteveBrief
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_SteveBrief
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Yesterday's Tile grid is working. Today the Board has to coordinate ships across those tiles. I've
      left an unfinished build in the IDE. Can you test its placement logic?
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_YouBrief
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_YouBrief
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: I'll check the occupied cells, edge cases, and whether the graphics match the data.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_SteveRule
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_SteveRule
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: 'One important rule: a rejected placement must leave the original board alone. Let me know when the
      build passes its checks.'
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_EndCall
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_EndCall
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_ArchitectIntro
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 14
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_ArchitectIntro
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: A Tile represents one cell. The Board owns the grid and coordinates operations that involve several
      cells. Let us start with the direction a ship grows.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_SentinelIntro
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_SentinelIntro
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: We can test privately without pretending everything works. Click the IDE, place a vertical ship, and
      watch which cells the code actually changes.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_Test0
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_Test0
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_OrientationReview
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1001
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_OrientationReview
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: A vertical ship changes its row for each segment; a horizontal ship changes its column. The Board
      keeps that row/column convention consistent.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants:
    - requiredLevel: 2
      lineText: The occupied-cell function separates board coordinates from pixels. Each segment is start + i times
        a direction vector; the tiles need not guess their neighbors.
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_OrientationCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_Test1
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_BoundsReview
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1001
    exerciseIndex: 1
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_BoundsReview
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: Checking the starting tile is not enough. Every segment needs a valid row and column before the Board
      reads or writes that tile.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants:
    - requiredLevel: 2
      lineText: The invariant is 0 <= row < rows and 0 <= column < columns for every segment. Equal-to-size is outside
        the array; test a rectangular board and both orientations.
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_BoundsCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_Test2
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_OverlapReview
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1001
    exerciseIndex: 2
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_OverlapReview
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: The broken loop wrote the first segments before discovering a collision. Checking the complete footprint
      first prevents half a ship from surviving a rejected placement.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants:
    - requiredLevel: 2
      lineText: 'Treat placement as a small transaction: construct the candidate cells, validate all of them, then
        commit the mutation. Failure preserves the previous board exactly.'
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_FriendMessage
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_Test3
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_RenderReview
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1001
    exerciseIndex: 3
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_RenderReview
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: The Board data was right, but the drawing used the wrong mapping. Columns become x, rows become y,
      and cellSize converts those units into pixels.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants:
    - requiredLevel: 2
      lineText: With the shape origin at its top-left and no board offset, setPosition({column * cellSize, row *
        cellSize}) aligns graphics to data. setSize describes the length along the correct axis.
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_RenderCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_OrientationCheck
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: If a ship is vertical, which coordinate changes for each segment?
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices:
    - choiceText: The row changes; the column stays fixed.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: D3_OrientationCorrect
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 1
    - choiceText: The column changes; the row stays fixed.
      personality: 4
      targetStepOnClick: D3_OrientationRetry
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 0
    nextStepID: ''
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_OrientationRetry
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: You've swapped the axes, Sentinel. Changing the column moves across the board; a vertical ship changes
      its row while keeping its column fixed.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_OrientationCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_OrientationCorrect
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: 'Exactly. Each segment advances one row down the board while staying in the same column. Next, try
      a ship near the bottom edge: its starting cell can be valid even when later segments are not.'
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_Test1
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: Day3.Board.Knowledge.Orientation
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_BoundsCheck
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: There are eight columns numbered from zero. Is column eight valid?
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices:
    - choiceText: There are eight columns, so column eight should fit.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: D3_BoundsRetry
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 0
    - choiceText: No. Valid columns are zero through seven.
      personality: 4
      targetStepOnClick: D3_BoundsCorrect
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 1
    nextStepID: ''
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_BoundsRetry
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: Architect, eight is the number of columns, not the last index. With zero-based indexing the columns
      are zero through seven, so column eight is outside the board.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_BoundsCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_BoundsCorrect
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: Good. Next we need to reject overlap without leaving partial changes. The existing ship is blue; try
      starting to its left.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_Test2
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: Day3.Board.Knowledge.Bounds
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_FriendMessage
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_OverlapCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1000
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
    message:
      messageId: 96233abcd9f14613a28008f6d99424ba
      contactKey: friend
      contactName: Friend
      portrait:
        fileID: 21300000
        guid: aa787758b18f479586e00f1ae714dd74
        type: 3
      text: Hey, how is the project going? Remember to take a break when you get a chance.
      replies:
      - text: Getting there. I found a bug and actually understand it now.
        response: That sounds like progress! Catch up after work?
        connectednessDelta: 5
        suspicionDelta: 0
      - text: Still testing. I'll message you later.
        response: No rush. Good luck with it!
        connectednessDelta: 0
        suspicionDelta: 0
      waitForReply: false
  - stepID: D3_OverlapCheck
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: Why did we separate validation from writing the cells?
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices:
    - choiceText: So failure cannot leave the board partly modified.
      personality: 4
      targetStepOnClick: D3_OverlapCorrect
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 1
    - choiceText: So the ship graphic draws faster.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: D3_OverlapRetry
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 0
    nextStepID: ''
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_OverlapRetry
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: Architect, drawing speed does not explain the leftover cells. Checking and writing one segment at
      a time can leave a partial ship behind; validate the entire footprint before writing any cells.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_OverlapCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_OverlapCorrect
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: Exactly. Validate every target cell first, then commit the placement. A rejected ship must leave the
      board unchanged; next we can check whether the SFML graphic matches those cells.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_Test3
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: Day3.Board.Knowledge.Atomicity
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_RenderCheck
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: The occupied cells are correct but the ship appears in the wrong place. Where should we investigate
      first?
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices:
    - choiceText: Change the occupied cells until they match the graphic.
      personality: 4
      targetStepOnClick: D3_RenderRetry
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 0
    - choiceText: The conversion from row/column to pixel position.
      personality: 2
      targetStepOnClick: D3_RenderCorrect
      suspicionChange: 0
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 1
    nextStepID: ''
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_RenderRetry
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: 'Sentinel, moving correct board data would only hide the drawing error. Keep the occupied cells and
      fix the SFML position: column becomes x and row becomes y, both scaled by cell size.'
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_RenderCheck
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_RenderCorrect
    speakerName: The Grand Architect
    personality: 2
    lineText: 'Exactly. Now run the whole build: orientation, boundaries, overlap, unchanged state on failure, and
      visual alignment.'
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_Final
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: Day3.Board.Knowledge.Rendering
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_Final
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_FinalVoices
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1001
    exerciseIndex: 4
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_FinalVoices
    speakerName: The Sentinel
    personality: 4
    lineText: 'The regression suite passes. You can use the same habit in Minesweeper: keep cell data consistent,
      protect array boundaries, and make the SFML view reflect that data.'
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_ReportCall
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_ReportCall
    speakerName: Me
    personality: 0
    lineText: ''
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_SteveQuestion
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 1
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_SteveQuestion
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: The build looks better. What prevented the overlap bug from leaving partial ships?
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices:
    - choiceText: I validate every target cell before writing any of them.
      personality: 0
      targetStepOnClick: D3_ReportGood
      suspicionChange: -5
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 1
    - choiceText: I made the ship sprite cover the leftover cells.
      personality: 0
      targetStepOnClick: D3_ReportClarify
      suspicionChange: 3
      requiredLevel: 0
      choiceGroup: ''
      personalityStatChange: 1
    nextStepID: ''
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 2
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_ReportGood
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Good. That gives us a reliable Board to build attacks on. Keep those regression cases for tomorrow.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_CloseFinalCall
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
  - stepID: D3_ReportClarify
    speakerName: Steve
    personality: 0
    lineText: Covering the cells would only hide it. The important fix was checking all cells before changing board
      data. Keep that distinction in mind.
    displayDuration: 4
    lineVariants: []
    choices: []
    nextStepID: D3_CloseFinalCall
    alternateNextStepID: ''
    awardSkillKey: ''
    narrativeEventKey: ''
    stepType: 0
    exerciseIndex: 0
    suspicionChange: 0
    delayDuration: 0
    NewSteveExpression: 0
    targetSceneName: Sleep
    steveChallenge:
      fileID: 0
